<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=alchemy">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Chemistry</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alchemy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alchemy is a philosophical and protoscientific tradition whose common aims were turning base metals into gold and making an elixir of immortality; in its Western form it is first attested in texts written in Greco-Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the first centuries CE, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> as its centre. Chinese and Indian alchemy appear to have been mostly independent in their earlier stages. Alchemy reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> through translations from Arabic from 1144 onwards, and the Latin tradition played a significant role in the development of early modern chemistry and medicine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alchemy.jpg" alt="Alchemy" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:E-codices_zbz-Ms-Rh-0172_044_max_copy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1st century CE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Alexandria</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/empire/roman-egypt">Roman Egypt</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>China (by 317 CE); India (2nd–5th centuries)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Whether the Western, Chinese and Indian traditions share an origin is an open question.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/distillation">Distillation<span>c. 1200 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">Gunpowder<span>808</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/chemical-revolution">Modern chemistry<span>1787</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=alchemy">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
